1
00:00:15,126 --> 00:00:16,835
Bong.

2
00:00:16,836 --> 00:00:19,713
Let us write it in stone.

3
00:00:19,714 --> 00:00:23,050
By God's will, we will prosper.

4
00:00:23,077 --> 00:00:25,496
We wouldn't have to slave
like carabaos [water buffalo].

5
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,764
We'll be the ones

6
00:00:28,765 --> 00:00:33,269
with workers to till the land for us.

7
00:00:33,728 --> 00:00:35,812
Oh, Tino.

8
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:37,147
Wake up!

9
00:00:37,148 --> 00:00:39,317
We still have much to harvest.

10
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:41,443
If we don't...

11
00:00:41,444 --> 00:00:43,070
they might scold us again.

12
00:00:43,071 --> 00:00:46,073
You can talk about your dreams later.

13
00:00:46,074 --> 00:00:47,909
The rain is coming.

14
00:00:49,535 --> 00:00:51,536
Tell me.

15
00:00:51,537 --> 00:00:54,207
Don't you have dreams?

16
00:00:54,957 --> 00:00:56,541
Even...

17
00:00:56,542 --> 00:00:59,337
to just get out of this town?

18
00:01:00,088 --> 00:01:02,964
Do you not want to...

19
00:01:02,965 --> 00:01:05,635
grow old with me?

20
00:01:05,968 --> 00:01:07,177
Tino.

21
00:01:07,178 --> 00:01:10,640
Let us become hacienderos
[landowners] here in San Nicolas.

22
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:14,685
Tino.

23
00:01:14,686 --> 00:01:17,146
I have a simple dream.

24
00:01:17,897 --> 00:01:21,942
I want to build our own restaurant.

25
00:01:21,943 --> 00:01:23,902
And...

26
00:01:23,903 --> 00:01:28,116
to own land we can farm.

27
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:34,497
And the ingredients we use
will come from that land as well.

28
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,210
I like that.

29
00:01:40,211 --> 00:01:41,628
Alright.

30
00:01:41,629 --> 00:01:44,048
Then that is my dream too.

31
00:01:44,632 --> 00:01:46,591
You are imitating me.

32
00:01:46,592 --> 00:01:47,759
I am.

33
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:51,973
So I can be certain you
and I will grow old together.

34
00:01:56,102 --> 00:01:57,185
I like that.

35
00:01:57,186 --> 00:01:58,770
No, you do not.

36
00:01:58,771 --> 00:01:59,730
I like it!

37
00:01:59,731 --> 00:02:01,107
Really?

38
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,900
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 3)

39
00:02:04,902 --> 00:02:06,988
Stop here.

40
00:02:46,152 --> 00:02:48,987
Here I thought we were
gonna do something...

41
00:02:48,988 --> 00:02:50,990
Other than this.

42
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,034
Why?

43
00:02:54,035 --> 00:02:57,163
What were you thinking?

44
00:03:00,416 --> 00:03:08,007
Is it true the restaurant won't
reopen until Grandpa Tino’s burial?

45
00:03:08,674 --> 00:03:10,301
Yes.

46
00:03:10,801 --> 00:03:16,098
It's what elders believe around here.

47
00:03:20,186 --> 00:03:22,229
Don't worry.

48
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:26,067
You still have a job when
the restaurant reopens.

49
00:03:27,652 --> 00:03:31,029
How about the other staff?

50
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:34,199
Everybody won’t get paid until you reopen?

51
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,533
Just you.

52
00:03:35,534 --> 00:03:37,327
You're the only one on probation.

53
00:03:37,328 --> 00:03:39,038
Oh, come on.

54
00:03:46,128 --> 00:03:48,171
I'm sorry.

55
00:03:48,172 --> 00:03:50,757
Grandpa Tino's gone

56
00:03:50,758 --> 00:03:54,095
and I'm worrying about other things.

57
00:03:58,683 --> 00:04:01,102
I'm sorry too.

58
00:04:03,729 --> 00:04:08,818
I don't know what to do now
that Grandpa’s gone.

59
00:04:10,403 --> 00:04:12,571
His whole life...

60
00:04:14,865 --> 00:04:18,493
He was in charge of this restaurant.

61
00:04:18,494 --> 00:04:21,289
He was the one we all followed.

62
00:04:27,211 --> 00:04:29,504
I think...

63
00:04:29,505 --> 00:04:33,383
You'll be our new manager.

64
00:04:33,384 --> 00:04:35,136
I know, right?

65
00:04:36,721 --> 00:04:38,264
I don't know.

66
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,475
I wish.

67
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:43,978
But...

68
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:50,567
I’m sure my family will fight over this.

69
00:04:50,568 --> 00:04:52,068
I have to tell you something, Jorge.

70
00:04:52,069 --> 00:04:55,489
But don't get mad.

71
00:04:57,616 --> 00:05:02,704
Don't you think you're too young
to become a manager?

72
00:05:02,705 --> 00:05:06,291
Don't you need to finish college first?

73
00:05:06,292 --> 00:05:08,293
You know, Kiko...

74
00:05:08,294 --> 00:05:12,797
Grandpa Tino didn't have to study
to build this restaurant.

75
00:05:12,798 --> 00:05:15,968
And he made it grow.

76
00:05:17,636 --> 00:05:22,474
You don't need to study
to be successful in life.

77
00:05:22,475 --> 00:05:25,560
It's because you're rich.

78
00:05:25,561 --> 00:05:27,897
For me...

79
00:05:29,607 --> 00:05:33,860
It's important to have education.

80
00:05:33,861 --> 00:05:38,908
It's more fulfilling to
have finished something.

81
00:06:01,222 --> 00:06:02,555
So...

82
00:06:02,556 --> 00:06:05,434
Should I bring you home?

83
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:28,958
Kiko, can I sleep at your house?

84
00:06:29,792 --> 00:06:33,253
I kinda don’t want to see my dad.

85
00:06:33,254 --> 00:06:39,050
And our house feels too...

86
00:06:39,051 --> 00:06:40,636
Sad?

87
00:06:41,554 --> 00:06:43,180
Chaotic.

88
00:06:45,224 --> 00:06:46,725
But Jorge...

89
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:50,019
Our house is small.

90
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:52,106
I don’t care if it's small.

91
00:06:52,648 --> 00:06:55,609
Size doesn't matter.

92
00:06:56,026 --> 00:06:57,528
Huh?

93
00:06:59,071 --> 00:06:59,914
Huh?

94
00:07:00,182 --> 00:07:01,124
Huh?

95
00:07:03,075 --> 00:07:05,035
You don't mind if it’s small?

96
00:07:08,247 --> 00:07:10,081
Oh.

97
00:07:10,082 --> 00:07:11,958
Actually...

98
00:07:11,959 --> 00:07:14,169
Mine isn't that small.

99
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:18,214
But I live in my Aunt’s house now.

100
00:07:18,215 --> 00:07:20,384
Oh, I see.

101
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,642
I don’t mind.

102
00:07:32,646 --> 00:07:34,607
Let's go?

103
00:07:43,991 --> 00:07:45,701
Ouch!

104
00:07:49,371 --> 00:07:52,082
You weren’t being careful.

105
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:56,169
So, it's my fault now?
I'm the one who got hurt.

106
00:07:56,170 --> 00:07:58,546
Then what, is it my motorcycle's fault?

107
00:07:58,547 --> 00:08:02,426
- Come on!
- I can walk!

108
00:08:07,097 --> 00:08:08,139
It hurts.

109
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:09,099
Can you do it?

110
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,434
Yes.

111
00:08:21,570 --> 00:08:23,821
It stings.

112
00:08:23,822 --> 00:08:26,158
Still hurts?

113
00:08:27,034 --> 00:08:29,661
Manong Kiko?

114
00:08:29,662 --> 00:08:31,664
These are my cousins.

115
00:08:32,998 --> 00:08:34,708
Jorge.

116
00:08:35,417 --> 00:08:36,584
This is...

117
00:08:36,585 --> 00:08:37,961
Jasmine

118
00:08:37,962 --> 00:08:39,755
and Samantha.

119
00:08:40,881 --> 00:08:45,261
Can you get some ice and the first aid kit?

120
00:08:48,013 --> 00:08:50,808
They're the ones who wait for me
when I come home.

121
00:08:51,850 --> 00:08:55,062
They open the door for me.

122
00:08:57,273 --> 00:08:58,856
Can I see?

123
00:08:58,857 --> 00:09:00,818
Does it still hurt?

124
00:09:01,443 --> 00:09:03,028
- Yes.
- Jasmine?

125
00:09:08,450 --> 00:09:10,076
Thank you.

126
00:09:10,077 --> 00:09:13,872
Manong Kiko, is he your boyfriend?

127
00:09:16,458 --> 00:09:18,377
Ask him.

128
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:24,215
I can be like an older brother too.

129
00:09:24,216 --> 00:09:27,678
Will you also give us chocolates?

130
00:09:30,681 --> 00:09:31,890
Yes.

131
00:09:31,891 --> 00:09:34,435
Lots and lots of chocolates.

132
00:09:36,562 --> 00:09:37,562
Go to sleep.

133
00:09:37,563 --> 00:09:40,356
Don't wait for your mom anymore.

134
00:09:40,357 --> 00:09:42,860
Go now. It's already late.

135
00:09:50,784 --> 00:09:52,786
Does it hurt here?

136
00:09:54,538 --> 00:09:57,665
Who gives them chocolates?

137
00:09:57,666 --> 00:09:59,335
Oh, that?

138
00:10:00,169 --> 00:10:01,920
Don’t mind that.

139
00:10:05,466 --> 00:10:07,926
Your helmet's still on.

140
00:10:09,011 --> 00:10:09,845
Oh, right.

141
00:10:09,846 --> 00:10:11,889
You're crazy.

142
00:10:16,935 --> 00:10:18,354
Oh.

143
00:10:20,773 --> 00:10:23,608
You have plans to study again.

144
00:10:23,609 --> 00:10:25,568
Don't look at that.

145
00:10:25,569 --> 00:10:28,322
I happened to see it while passing by.

146
00:10:29,907 --> 00:10:31,700
Just like that?

147
00:10:32,743 --> 00:10:34,494
I had plans.

148
00:10:34,495 --> 00:10:36,788
But...

149
00:10:36,789 --> 00:10:40,792
My dad died early.

150
00:10:40,793 --> 00:10:43,420
So it was mom who took care of us.

151
00:10:44,755 --> 00:10:47,383
But she had a hard time.

152
00:10:48,342 --> 00:10:53,638
For now, I'm helping my cousins
‘til they finish high school.

153
00:10:53,639 --> 00:10:56,183
Then I'll go back to studying.

154
00:10:57,184 --> 00:10:59,936
But they're still so young!

155
00:10:59,937 --> 00:11:03,856
Jasmine is still in third grade.

156
00:11:03,857 --> 00:11:05,400
Wow.

157
00:11:05,401 --> 00:11:12,366
You talk like you finished school yourself.

158
00:11:21,375 --> 00:11:25,546
Why didn't you try to
apply for scholarships?

159
00:11:28,424 --> 00:11:31,468
Who said I didn't try?

160
00:11:33,470 --> 00:11:37,432
When I graduated high school,

161
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:40,143
I applied for a scholarship.

162
00:11:40,144 --> 00:11:43,897
But I wasn’t so lucky.

163
00:11:44,398 --> 00:11:46,692
You know...

164
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:50,696
It hurts to be rejected.

165
00:11:52,948 --> 00:11:55,867
I've never been rejected.

166
00:11:55,868 --> 00:11:57,327
Okay, wow!

167
00:11:58,537 --> 00:12:02,206
Why don't you want to study anymore?

168
00:12:02,207 --> 00:12:04,751
How about we study in the same university?

169
00:12:04,752 --> 00:12:08,046
You just want to be with me in Manila.

170
00:12:09,923 --> 00:12:11,507
That would be good.

171
00:12:11,508 --> 00:12:13,384
And...

172
00:12:13,385 --> 00:12:16,180
If I run out of money,

173
00:12:17,264 --> 00:12:19,767
I can borrow from you.

174
00:12:22,352 --> 00:12:24,020
What's in it for me?

175
00:12:24,021 --> 00:12:25,396
Well...

176
00:12:25,397 --> 00:12:27,315
We'll always be together.

177
00:12:27,316 --> 00:12:32,236
And I'll do your assignments.

178
00:12:32,237 --> 00:12:34,655
Just that?

179
00:12:34,656 --> 00:12:36,783
What else do you want?

180
00:12:36,784 --> 00:12:40,077
How about dropping me off at the market?

181
00:12:40,078 --> 00:12:41,829
I'll cook.

182
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:43,581
Is that all?

183
00:12:43,582 --> 00:12:45,209
Deal.

184
00:12:48,337 --> 00:12:51,006
What else did you do?

185
00:12:52,925 --> 00:12:55,510
I was a working student.

186
00:12:55,511 --> 00:13:01,642
When I was sixteen, I
got my driver's license.

187
00:13:03,644 --> 00:13:09,775
And I borrowed a
motorcycle from Uncle Pilo.

188
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,529
Done.

189
00:13:16,198 --> 00:13:19,618
How about we go play basketball?

190
00:13:21,787 --> 00:13:24,580
What? It's already late.

191
00:13:24,581 --> 00:13:27,792
You're forgetting about my burnt leg.

192
00:13:27,793 --> 00:13:28,960
You'll do fine.

193
00:13:28,961 --> 00:13:31,128
It's cold outside.

194
00:13:31,129 --> 00:13:34,382
- Really, now?
- That one smells clean.

195
00:13:34,383 --> 00:13:36,385
Let’s go!

196
00:13:43,267 --> 00:13:45,602
Make sure you can handle me.

197
00:13:47,771 --> 00:13:48,938
Looks like you can.

198
00:13:48,939 --> 00:13:50,857
Oh.

199
00:13:50,858 --> 00:13:52,734
It's locked.

200
00:13:54,027 --> 00:13:55,612
Let's go home.

201
00:13:58,699 --> 00:14:00,033
Hey!

202
00:14:00,909 --> 00:14:02,327
Jorge.

203
00:14:03,036 --> 00:14:04,454
What?

204
00:14:12,462 --> 00:14:14,297
Forget the gate.

205
00:14:14,298 --> 00:14:15,590
Let's climb over.

206
00:14:15,591 --> 00:14:18,010
I'll help you.
Come on.

207
00:14:20,262 --> 00:14:20,721
No.

208
00:14:20,722 --> 00:14:22,847
- I'll help you.
- No.

209
00:14:22,848 --> 00:14:25,725
We’re gonna climb?
Over the fence?

210
00:14:25,726 --> 00:14:27,018
The patrol will see us.

211
00:14:27,019 --> 00:14:28,269
Come on!

212
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:29,813
We won’t get caught.

213
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,525
Come on.

214
00:14:34,151 --> 00:14:37,487
- I'll lift you up.
- I can do it.

215
00:14:55,213 --> 00:14:57,007
Told you so.

216
00:14:58,550 --> 00:15:00,843
You're acting like you don't want it.

217
00:15:00,844 --> 00:15:01,887
Huh?

218
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:05,724
You acted like you didn’t want to climb.

219
00:15:07,476 --> 00:15:10,020
- Come on.
- Alright, I'm climbing.

220
00:15:10,646 --> 00:15:11,855
I can do it.

221
00:15:14,483 --> 00:15:16,109
Easy!

222
00:15:18,779 --> 00:15:21,156
Here’s the ball.

223
00:15:27,579 --> 00:15:30,206
Sir, stop!

224
00:15:30,207 --> 00:15:32,250
Kiko!

225
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:35,003
Agnes?

226
00:15:36,296 --> 00:15:38,798
I was on my way to your house.

227
00:15:38,799 --> 00:15:40,549
I brought you stuff.

228
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:41,884
You just arrived?

229
00:15:41,885 --> 00:15:43,302
No.

230
00:15:43,303 --> 00:15:45,054
I arrived yesterday.

231
00:15:45,055 --> 00:15:47,598
Grandpa made me come home to San Nicolas,

232
00:15:47,599 --> 00:15:50,434
so I could fix Grandma's social security.

233
00:15:50,435 --> 00:15:52,771
You know, they're getting old.

234
00:15:53,438 --> 00:15:54,855
Who's that?

235
00:15:54,856 --> 00:15:56,691
- Uh, Jorge.
- Jorge.

236
00:15:56,692 --> 00:15:59,318
- This is Agnes.
- Yes.

237
00:15:59,319 --> 00:16:02,947
Agnes, this is Jorge.

238
00:16:02,948 --> 00:16:06,076
Hello, I'm Kiko's girlfriend.

239
00:16:07,953 --> 00:16:08,829
Uh... she's...

240
00:16:08,830 --> 00:16:13,541
Come with me to your house.
You can help me carry the stuff I brought.

241
00:16:13,542 --> 00:16:15,711
Is your aunt home?

242
00:16:16,378 --> 00:16:18,004
Not yet.

243
00:16:18,005 --> 00:16:19,422
She'll be home late.

244
00:16:19,423 --> 00:16:22,925
Let's go together then.

245
00:16:22,926 --> 00:16:25,761
Go ahead.
I'm going home too.

246
00:16:25,762 --> 00:16:29,932
Invite your friend.
He can come with us.

247
00:16:29,933 --> 00:16:31,727
No, it's alright.

248
00:16:32,644 --> 00:16:34,937
- Let's go, Kiko.
- I'm going the other way.

249
00:16:34,938 --> 00:16:37,899
Let's go.

250
00:16:40,485 --> 00:16:41,862
Ride in the back.

251
00:17:36,875 --> 00:17:40,211
Sir, happy anniversary!

252
00:17:40,212 --> 00:17:42,714
Happy anniversary!

253
00:17:44,758 --> 00:17:45,717
Kiko.

254
00:17:45,718 --> 00:17:48,803
You know, in Manila...

255
00:17:48,804 --> 00:17:52,681
Our team leader promoted
me to a higher position.

256
00:17:52,682 --> 00:17:56,769
Now, I have the opportunity
to become a team leader too.

257
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:58,479
Things are great in Manila, Kiko.

258
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:02,108
And there are a lot of Ilocanos there.

259
00:18:02,109 --> 00:18:06,487
This is good for both of us, Kiko.

260
00:18:06,488 --> 00:18:08,781
We're still in a relationship?

261
00:18:08,782 --> 00:18:14,371
I promised I would
visit every chance I got.

262
00:18:15,288 --> 00:18:19,875
And I said that if you
choose to work in Manila,

263
00:18:19,876 --> 00:18:21,418
then it's over between us.

264
00:18:21,419 --> 00:18:24,463
But I never agreed to that, Kiko.

265
00:18:24,464 --> 00:18:29,844
Why do you think I keep
sending gifts to your aunt and cousins?

266
00:18:29,845 --> 00:18:32,806
It's been over for us, Agnes.

267
00:18:35,809 --> 00:18:38,227
For you, Kiko.

268
00:18:38,228 --> 00:18:40,688
Not for me.

269
00:18:40,689 --> 00:18:42,273
Why?

270
00:18:42,274 --> 00:18:44,651
Is there somebody else?

271
00:18:45,986 --> 00:18:48,445
You chose your job over me.

272
00:18:48,446 --> 00:18:50,740
I begged you.

273
00:18:51,616 --> 00:18:53,993
Just so you wouldn't leave.

274
00:18:53,994 --> 00:18:56,704
I needed to, Kiko.

275
00:18:56,705 --> 00:18:58,998
I had to listen to my parents.

276
00:18:58,999 --> 00:19:01,792
And that was a job opportunity, Kiko.

277
00:19:01,793 --> 00:19:04,420
Do you remember how
we couldn't afford places like this?

278
00:19:04,421 --> 00:19:07,549
We had no money.

279
00:19:08,717 --> 00:19:11,677
But now we do.

280
00:19:11,678 --> 00:19:16,348
I'll take care of our expenses
while you look for a job, Kiko.

281
00:19:16,349 --> 00:19:18,642
I tried my best, Agnes.

282
00:19:18,643 --> 00:19:22,647
So I could've provided for you.

283
00:19:25,567 --> 00:19:29,361
That's not what I mean, Kiko.

284
00:19:29,362 --> 00:19:31,614
What I wanted to say was,

285
00:19:31,615 --> 00:19:35,452
Come with me to Manila.
Let's start over.

286
00:19:36,328 --> 00:19:38,496
Let's start over, Kiko.

287
00:19:40,874 --> 00:19:43,210
I don’t want to, Agnes.

288
00:19:49,966 --> 00:19:52,636
Is it because of Jorge?

289
00:19:53,929 --> 00:19:56,764
There's no one else, Agnes.

290
00:19:56,765 --> 00:19:59,225
You left me.

291
00:19:59,226 --> 00:20:01,978
We're done.

292
00:20:42,394 --> 00:20:44,728
Come here, Kiko.
Look at this.

293
00:20:44,729 --> 00:20:46,648
Look at what Agnes gave us.

294
00:20:47,941 --> 00:20:49,276
Auntie...

295
00:20:50,026 --> 00:20:51,611
Put them back.

296
00:20:52,153 --> 00:20:55,322
Agnes and I are over, auntie.

297
00:20:55,323 --> 00:20:59,994
I don't even know why
she's still giving you gifts.

298
00:20:59,995 --> 00:21:01,496
Why?

299
00:21:02,414 --> 00:21:04,916
Agnes is such a great girl.

300
00:21:05,792 --> 00:21:07,584
Look at these.

301
00:21:07,585 --> 00:21:10,963
She gave notebooks to your cousins.

302
00:21:10,964 --> 00:21:15,927
Auntie, please stop.

303
00:21:17,470 --> 00:21:22,516
Can't I decide what's best for me here?

304
00:21:22,517 --> 00:21:24,018
Why?

305
00:21:24,019 --> 00:21:25,978
What's your plan for yourself?

306
00:21:25,979 --> 00:21:28,897
The restaurant closed.

307
00:21:28,898 --> 00:21:31,484
What even are these?

308
00:21:31,901 --> 00:21:35,322
You’re always searching.

309
00:21:37,449 --> 00:21:40,577
Always writing down...

310
00:21:41,202 --> 00:21:44,039
But you never send them.

311
00:22:44,349 --> 00:22:46,935
- Since when?
- What?

312
00:22:49,854 --> 00:22:53,440
That you’re falling in love with Kiko?

313
00:22:53,441 --> 00:22:56,151
Who said I'm falling for him?

314
00:22:56,152 --> 00:22:57,903
You know,

315
00:22:57,904 --> 00:23:00,824
This is the part where you're in denial.

316
00:23:01,449 --> 00:23:02,658
Take that.

317
00:23:02,659 --> 00:23:07,329
Take that pot. Take it.

318
00:23:07,330 --> 00:23:09,873
Yes, boss.
Wait up. It's heavy.

319
00:23:09,874 --> 00:23:12,126
Like your feelings?

320
00:23:12,127 --> 00:23:15,547
- Can you stop, Ruth?
- Hmm. In denial.

321
00:23:16,673 --> 00:23:19,299
Who caught feelings first?

322
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:24,012
If you don't shut up,
I'll hit you with this pot.

323
00:23:24,013 --> 00:23:24,639
You want that?

324
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:26,975
Hurry over here.

325
00:23:29,185 --> 00:23:30,686
Auntie, how many have been made?

326
00:23:30,687 --> 00:23:33,397
Eleven ma’am.

327
00:23:33,398 --> 00:23:34,607
Eleven.

328
00:23:35,191 --> 00:23:36,733
How many days did you make this?

329
00:23:36,734 --> 00:23:39,278
Three to four days, ma’am.

330
00:23:39,279 --> 00:23:41,531
Three to four days.

331
00:23:43,616 --> 00:23:44,826
But...

332
00:23:46,035 --> 00:23:48,997
What do you like about him?

333
00:23:49,497 --> 00:23:50,747
You know, Ruth.

334
00:23:50,748 --> 00:23:52,875
I don't care about him.

335
00:23:52,876 --> 00:23:54,835
See?

336
00:23:54,836 --> 00:23:57,463
My professor said, that's the next stage.

337
00:23:57,464 --> 00:23:59,047
It's called anger.

338
00:23:59,048 --> 00:24:02,593
You'll get mad at him.
You're angry at him.

339
00:24:02,594 --> 00:24:04,762
Take that and put it there.

340
00:24:05,638 --> 00:24:08,515
- How many pots were damaged?
- Eight, ma'am.

341
00:24:08,516 --> 00:24:10,143
Eight.

342
00:24:12,270 --> 00:24:14,146
Please take care of it, Auntie.

343
00:24:14,147 --> 00:24:18,025
- The pots need to be perfect when we sell them.
- Of course, ma'am. I can do it.

344
00:24:18,026 --> 00:24:20,737
- Really?
- It's easy, ma'am.

345
00:24:22,572 --> 00:24:24,699
Okay, Auntie.

346
00:24:31,998 --> 00:24:35,667
Oops. That's enough.

347
00:24:35,668 --> 00:24:38,921
You're not supposed
to be the first to call.

348
00:24:38,922 --> 00:24:41,007
Let him make the first move.

349
00:24:43,426 --> 00:24:48,096
You learned a lot from your teacher, huh?
You know too much.

350
00:24:48,097 --> 00:24:50,182
- Look at you.
- I know right.

351
00:24:50,183 --> 00:24:54,603
My professor even said, "Ruth,
you were born to be a psychologist."

352
00:24:54,604 --> 00:24:57,022
Mm. See!

353
00:24:57,023 --> 00:24:58,524
Okay, okay.

354
00:24:58,525 --> 00:25:00,443
I believe you now.

355
00:25:01,903 --> 00:25:03,987
What's the next stage?

356
00:25:03,988 --> 00:25:05,489
See?

357
00:25:05,490 --> 00:25:06,740
Bargaining.

358
00:25:06,741 --> 00:25:08,993
You'll start begging.

359
00:25:10,328 --> 00:25:12,788
Auntie, why does that have a crack?

360
00:25:12,789 --> 00:25:16,833
If there's a mistake,
we can fix it so it looks better.

361
00:25:16,834 --> 00:25:20,796
How many days will it take to make it?

362
00:25:20,797 --> 00:25:23,382
One day, ma'am.

363
00:25:23,383 --> 00:25:26,761
- How many have been made already?
- Fifty pieces, ma'am.

364
00:25:28,054 --> 00:25:30,013
Ruth.

365
00:25:30,014 --> 00:25:33,016
What does that mean?

366
00:25:33,017 --> 00:25:34,686
Like...

367
00:25:35,770 --> 00:25:39,731
You'll do everything
just for him to come back.

368
00:25:39,732 --> 00:25:41,024
But you know,

369
00:25:41,025 --> 00:25:45,779
it's better to confirm if
Agnes and Kiko are really a thing.

370
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:51,243
So you have a reason to forget about him.

371
00:25:51,244 --> 00:25:54,913
But he's still cute, right?

372
00:25:54,914 --> 00:25:58,293
What a wasted opportunity.

373
00:26:01,087 --> 00:26:03,297
My god, Ruth.

374
00:26:03,298 --> 00:26:06,341
Where is this coming from?

375
00:26:06,342 --> 00:26:07,509
Wait.

376
00:26:07,510 --> 00:26:09,511
OMG.

377
00:26:09,512 --> 00:26:11,805
I have an idea. Hurry up.

378
00:26:11,806 --> 00:26:14,349
- What is it?
- Take it. Hurry.

379
00:26:14,350 --> 00:26:16,268
Hurry up. Carry that.

380
00:26:16,269 --> 00:26:19,813
- You know it's hot, right?
- Just take it.

381
00:26:19,814 --> 00:26:21,565
I have an idea.

382
00:26:21,566 --> 00:26:23,026
Wait.

383
00:26:25,945 --> 00:26:28,239
Hurry up!

384
00:26:34,245 --> 00:26:37,039
How about you help me?

385
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:39,625
What are you going to do with these?

386
00:26:39,626 --> 00:26:40,917
I’ll show you.

387
00:26:40,918 --> 00:26:42,878
Hold this.

388
00:26:42,879 --> 00:26:45,048
- What?
- Hold it.

389
00:26:46,299 --> 00:26:47,674
Repeat after me.

390
00:26:47,675 --> 00:26:49,635
The first one to fall,

391
00:26:49,636 --> 00:26:51,345
loses.

392
00:26:51,346 --> 00:26:52,889
Say it.

393
00:26:53,389 --> 00:26:55,975
The first one to fall, loses.

394
00:26:56,643 --> 00:26:57,976
Not like that.

395
00:26:57,977 --> 00:26:59,645
Like this.

396
00:26:59,646 --> 00:27:01,647
The first one to fall,

397
00:27:01,648 --> 00:27:03,566
loses!

398
00:27:05,860 --> 00:27:08,737
- That's such a waste.
- Those are already damaged.

399
00:27:08,738 --> 00:27:10,865
Your turn.

400
00:27:14,410 --> 00:27:16,244
The first one to fall,

401
00:27:16,245 --> 00:27:18,206
loses!

402
00:27:21,209 --> 00:27:22,542
No.

403
00:27:22,543 --> 00:27:23,877
Like this.

404
00:27:23,878 --> 00:27:26,588
The first one to fall,

405
00:27:26,589 --> 00:27:28,633
- Loses.
- Wait.

406
00:27:29,884 --> 00:27:31,803
Let me.

407
00:27:35,556 --> 00:27:37,724
The first one to fall,

408
00:27:37,725 --> 00:27:39,143
loses!

409
00:27:42,397 --> 00:27:43,855
Just like that.

410
00:27:43,856 --> 00:27:45,191
Again.

411
00:27:46,275 --> 00:27:47,860
Take it.

412
00:27:49,237 --> 00:27:50,529
Together.

413
00:27:50,530 --> 00:27:52,072
- The first one to fall,
- The first one to fall,

414
00:27:52,073 --> 00:27:54,033
- loses!
- loses!

415
00:28:00,206 --> 00:28:01,456
Good job.

416
00:28:01,457 --> 00:28:02,457
Well?

417
00:28:02,458 --> 00:28:04,251
Right?

418
00:28:04,252 --> 00:28:06,212
I told you.

419
00:28:12,635 --> 00:28:15,721
Francisco Cablayan?

420
00:28:15,722 --> 00:28:16,681
Ma'am.

421
00:28:16,682 --> 00:28:17,764
Scholarship?

422
00:28:17,765 --> 00:28:19,434
Yes, ma'am.

423
00:28:33,114 --> 00:28:39,536
Friends, the mayor is here.
He's arrived. They're here.

424
00:28:39,537 --> 00:28:43,373
Insiong, the mayor is here.

425
00:28:43,374 --> 00:28:47,377
Of course, that's the mayor.

426
00:28:47,378 --> 00:28:48,212
I don’t see him.

427
00:28:48,213 --> 00:28:50,422
He’s there, parking the car.

428
00:28:50,423 --> 00:28:53,050
Jorge, you have a visitor.

429
00:28:55,386 --> 00:28:57,805
Maybe it's Kiko.

430
00:28:58,806 --> 00:29:00,307
So what?

431
00:29:00,308 --> 00:29:03,226
Jorge, remember what we did.

432
00:29:03,227 --> 00:29:04,770
Don't forget.

433
00:29:04,771 --> 00:29:07,314
Love is for the weak.

434
00:29:07,315 --> 00:29:09,191
The first one to fall...

435
00:29:09,192 --> 00:29:10,109
- Loses.
- Loses.

436
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:11,110
Yeah, I know.

437
00:29:11,111 --> 00:29:13,321
Good.

438
00:29:26,459 --> 00:29:31,463
Hey, he's waving at you.

439
00:29:31,464 --> 00:29:33,633
He's smiling at you.

440
00:29:38,721 --> 00:29:41,140
He's so handsome.
